# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAT-AI .gitignore
#
# RULE: satellite data NEVER enters git history. One accidental 1 GB GRD commit
# poisons the repository permanently -- `git rm` does not reclaim the space,
# every future clone pays for it, and GitHub rejects pushes over 100 MB per file.
# The pre-commit large-file hook is the second line of defence.
# What IS committed: data/manifests/ (what we downloaded) and data/samples/
# (small demo assets), so the repo is reproducible without the data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Data ---
data/raw/**
data/processed/**
data/interim/**
!data/**/.gitkeep
!data/manifests/**
!data/samples/**
# The inference run's own record: which checkpoint, which chips, which
# threshold, how much area. Kilobytes of JSON, and the evidence behind every
# inference number quoted in the README -- the rasters it describes stay out.
#
# The directory re-inclusion is load-bearing: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a negation for a file inside one never matches. The
# `*.tif` rule below still keeps the rasters out.
!data/processed/**/
!data/processed/flood/*_metadata.json
!data/processed/flood/prediction_manifest.json
!data/processed/district_impact/*.json
!data/processed/exposure/*.json

# Raster / vector / archive formats, wherever they appear
*.tif
*.tiff
*.img
*.jp2
*.nc
*.hdf
*.h5
*.grib
*.grib2
*.safe/
*.SAFE/
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.7z
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.gpkg
*.parquet
*.feather
# ...but allow small committed demo assets
!data/samples/**/*.tif
!data/samples/**/*.gpkg
!data/samples/**/*.parquet

# --- Models / experiment outputs ---
models/**
# ...except the records that make a run identifiable and reproducible. The
# weights are large and regenerable; the manifest, the metrics and the fitted
# normalisation statistics are small and are the only evidence that a reported
# number came from a real run.
!models/*/
!models/**/*.json
!models/**/*.png

!models/.gitkeep
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.h5
ml/experiments/**/checkpoints/
mlruns/
wandb/

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
service-account*.json
.earthengine/
.netrc
.cdsapirc

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
eggs/
.eggs/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.installed.cfg
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# --- Testing / typing / linting caches ---
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.tox/
.nox/

# --- Notebooks ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/
notebooks/**/*.ipynb_convert*

# --- Node / Next.js (frontend) ---
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.vercel/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Editors / OS ---
.claude/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Docker / local infra ---
.docker-data/
postgres-data/

# --- Logs ---
logs/
*.log
